  "instructions": [
    "Heat 1 tbsp oil in a 12 inch nonstick skillet over medium heat. Add the onion and cook 3 minutes, until soft.",
    "Stir in the garlic and cumin and cook 30 seconds. Add the diced tomatoes with their juice and 1/4 tsp salt, and simmer 5 minutes until slightly thickened. Spoon this salsa into a bowl and wipe the skillet clean.",
    "Mash about a third of the black beans with a fork in a small bowl, then stir in the rest of the beans.",
    "Warm the beans in a small saucepan over low heat for 3 minutes, stirring now and then.",
    "Heat 1 tbsp oil in the skillet over medium heat. Warm the tortillas 4 at a time for 30 seconds per side until soft and lightly crisp at the edges, adding a little oil as needed, and stack on a plate under foil.",
    "Add the remaining oil to the skillet over medium-low heat. Crack in the eggs and cook 3 to 4 minutes, until the whites are fully set and the yolks are as firm as you like.",
    "Season the eggs with the remaining salt and the pepper.",
    "Spread beans on each tortilla, top with an egg, spoon on the salsa, and sprinkle with cheese. Serve 2 tortillas per person right away."
  ],
